    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23052" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-exhaustus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unexhausted</i> (<b>poet.</b> and
			post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metalla,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 174</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbes,</span>”
				<i>not plundered</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 686</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pubertas,</span>”
				<i>not enfeebled</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. G.
					20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				H. 5, 7</span></i> (but not in <i><span class="en">Cic. Fin. 3,
				2, 7</span></i>; v. Madv. ad h. l.).</div>
